From 26d65c68d636aff94d508ac81d3b491e7afbc4f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:10:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 399/406] Part: --export-web leaves out or simplifies parts,
 and warns of a page over 30 MB

A page of 54 MB (a third of it bolts) was stopped by a company PC's
antivirus. --web-exclude "pattern,..." leaves parts out (labels or
names of parts or of their groups); --web-simplify fasteners (or
patterns) draws bolts, nuts, washers and screws as cylinders along their
largest round face (shank and head) or boxes, coarse and without edges
(threaded bolts: about 1/100). Over 30 MB the export says so, with the
heaviest groups.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
